.TH git-harvest-id-update 1  "update " 
.SH NAME
git\-harvest\-id\-update \- Change a registered contributor\*(Aqs names, e\-mails or URLs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-harvest id update\fR [\fB\-\-rename\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-add\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-primary\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-primary\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-primary\-url\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIALIAS\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a registered contributor\*(Aqs names, e\-mails or URLs.
.PP
Changes an already\-registered contributor\*(Aqs names, e\-mail addresses or URLs, promotes one of them to primary, or renames the contributor\*(Aqs alias — every requested change is validated together and applied in one atomic write, or none of them are.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-rename\fR \fI<RENAME>\fR
Rename the contributor; the new alias must be unregistered
.TP
\fB\-\-add\-name\fR \fI<ADD_NAME>\fR
Add a name; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\-name\fR \fI<REMOVE_NAME>\fR
Remove a name; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-add\-email\fR \fI<ADD_EMAIL>\fR
Add an e\-mail address; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\-email\fR \fI<REMOVE_EMAIL>\fR
Remove an e\-mail address; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-add\-url\fR \fI<ADD_URL>\fR
Add a URL; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-remove\-url\fR \fI<REMOVE_URL>\fR
Remove a URL; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-primary\-name\fR \fI<PRIMARY_NAME>\fR
Make this name the primary, adding it if absent
.TP
\fB\-\-primary\-email\fR \fI<PRIMARY_EMAIL>\fR
Make this e\-mail the primary, adding it if absent
.TP
\fB\-\-primary\-url\fR \fI<PRIMARY_URL>\fR
Make this URL the primary, adding it if absent
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIALIAS\fR>
The contributor to change
